// the crew store's shelf
== hobby.store.draw
- Sketchpad and pencils · 15 credits
== hobby.store.knit
- Needles and wool · 12 credits
== hobby.store.puzzle
- Puzzle book · 10 credits

// crew near you who share the hobby (bubbles)
== hobby.share.read
- What are you reading? Any good?
- Oh, a fellow reader. Swap when you're done?
- Is that a good one? You're smiling at it.
== hobby.share.write
- Writing home? I owe my lot a letter.
- Journal? Me too. Every night, nearly.
== hobby.share.games
- What are you playing? Is it the one with the blocks?
- I'm stuck on level nine. Don't tell me.   #funny
== hobby.share.draw
- Can I see? Oh, that's good. Really good.
- You draw too? We should sketch the garden sometime.
== hobby.share.knit
- You knit too? Show me that stitch.
- Ooh, what are you making? Lovely colour.
- Another knitter. Zeke will be thrilled.   #funny
== hobby.share.puzzle
- Stuck? Seven across is "orbit". Sorry, sorry.   #funny
- Puzzle book? Which page are you on?
== hobby.share.stars
- That bright one? A whole cluster. Pretty, isn't it?
- Best seat on the ship, this. Mind if I join you?

== hobby.button
- Hobby

== tip.hobby
- Hobbies fill your leisure. Read, write, play games or watch a film on your device anywhere. Drawing, knitting and puzzles need supplies from the crew store on Deck 3; Zeke might teach you to knit.

== tip.offshift
- Off shift. Your evening is yours: call home from the booths on Deck 3, go to a ship tradition (Calendar), talk a while with someone, or try a hobby.

== tip.eve.talk
- Tap someone and choose Talk a while. A proper chat builds friendship much faster than a hello.

== tip.eve.hobby
- Try a hobby tonight: your device has Read, Write, Play games and Watch a film. Anywhere you can sit or stand still.

== tip.eve.trad
- {n} traditions on tonight. You can't go to them all, so pick one. They're on your Calendar.

== tip.eve.call
- Your people at home would love to hear from you. The call booths are on Deck 3.

== ideas.title
- Ideas for tonight

== ideas.trad
- {trad} at {time}

== ideas.friend
- {name} is in the {room}. Say hello?

== ideas.hobby
- Try a hobby: {hobby}

== ideas.booth
- A call booth is free on Deck 3

== ideas.none
- A quiet one. Read a bit, or get an early night.

== settle.clothes
- Change your clothes
== settle.hobby
- Try a hobby
== settle.talk
- Talk a while with someone

// Gardening as a hobby (the user's, via lead 10): hobby id 'garden', tending a bed in the hydroponics garden (Deck 3).
// Same keys as the other hobbies.
== tip.garden
- The garden's yours off shift too. Tending a bed counts as a hobby: it fills your leisure.
== hobby.name.garden
- Tend a bed
== hobby.start.garden
- Tending the bed...
- Watering, weeding, humming...
== hobby.done.garden
- The bed looks tidier. The leaves look happier.
- Your hands smell of soil and mint. Lovely.
== hobby.record.garden
- You tend the garden.
== hobby.share.garden
- Grab a trowel. That bed's been waiting for you.
- You garden too? The beans like a chat, I swear.   #funny
- Gently with the roots. There you go. Lovely.

